{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans","id":982457,"title":"[2E] Help me design the Courts of New Orleans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-05T17:29:22-07:00","id":982457,"title":"[2E] Help me design the Courts of New Orleans","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I'm presently running a crossover game set in New Orleans, vaguely inspired by The Originals, True Blood and the official VtR material. I'm having a lot of fun devising a multilayered city, but I've got stuck with Changeling. I've read the Court Creation playtest material, but I still struggle to understand exactly how the bulwark and Courts function in-game.<br /> <br /> Now, let me show what I've got so far:<ul><li>The Bulwark and theme of the Courts is, of course, about Mardi Gras.</li> <li>Each Court is called a Krewe here in the city, and each one is led by a Rex or Regina (King or Queen, respectively).</li> <li>There are three Courts: the Court of the Cross is the Court of Faith; its color is green; its emotion is Devotion. The Court of the Coin is the Court of Power; its color is gold; its emotion is Pride. The Indian Court is the Court of Justice; its color is purple; its emotion is Outrage.</li> <li>I imagine the Bulwark having taking place during Mardi Gras, perhaps as an elaborate competition between the masked members of the Courts and the Huntsmen. Maybe the Lost have to chase their Icons hidden among baubbles and throws. Maybe they invite the Gentry to an elaborate Ball, hoping to trick them into accepting a challenge doomed to failure.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Any help would be greatly appreciated. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 10-14-2021, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:42:35-07:00","id":982479,"title":"","content":"So, in other words. Mardi Gras is a time the Changelings dread. Neat reversal!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:41:25-07:00","id":982513,"title":"","content":"Mardi Gras is a time for both dread and anticipation. They say there are only two seasons in New Orleans: before Mardi Gras, and after Mardi Gras. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:04:22-07:00","id":982619,"title":"","content":"Interesting! I previously, after we got Toronto, tried to make. Freehold for New Orleans. I can't quite recall what I did for Courts. I think I had one centered on tourism and one on Mardi Gras's status as a trading hub/port town? The Courts of Work and Revelry, or something like that.<br /> I want to hear more about how your courts work, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:12:22-07:00","id":983294,"title":"","content":"I can't really help much on the Courts themselves, but I am open to helping work up ideas for NPCs in the Freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:48:35-07:00","id":983316,"title":"","content":"Keep the Bulwark simple, its IS Mardi Gras.<br /> <br /> So to maintain the Bulwark every year the Freehold maintains and protects the traditions of Mardi Gras with each court having its main area of responsiblity.<br /> <br /> The Court of Devotion focuses on protecting the religious end of things and particapates in the more religious elements.<br /> <br /> The Court of Outrage focuses on the Parade and Partying, making sure the parade goes ahead as schuedule, that the police don't interfer with people flashing for beads, that the city doesn't run out of booze.<br /> <br /> And the Court of Coins makes sure the Tourists visit, that politicians don't fuck things up, and the New Orleans businesses are prepared.<br /> <br /> So what the Huntsmen and enemy courts do to cause the Bulwark to fail is to cause Mardi Gras to fail, get the parade cancelled, have police crack down on public nudity, cut off the cities supply of booze, stir up hurricanes so no one visits, discourage the religious from observing the spiritual elements of Mardi Gras. In other words they try and sabotage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:49:58-07:00","id":983317,"title":"","content":"What do you have planned for the mantles for each court?<br /> <br /> I suggest \u2022\u2022\u2022 tokens for the 5th dot of each mantle, a Token Cross/Crusifix for the Court of Devotion, Purple Beads Token for the Court of Outrage, and Coin Token for the Court of Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-07-2016, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:37:48-07:00","id":983369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983316#post983316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep the Bulwark simple, its IS Mardi Gras.<br /> <br /> So to maintain the Bulwark every year the Freehold maintains and protects the traditions of Mardi Gras with each court having its main area of responsiblity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this option really ignores lots of opportunities and goes with the first thing anyone associates with New Orleans.<br /> <br /> Take a step back, think on what's important to the city's history and what would be important to the Changelings.<b> Honoring the dead</b> and <b>food </b>are the two things I think of, first. I'm envisioning a frequent (monthly, perhaps) ritual that borrows from Dia de los Muertos, where changelings place offerings of food at the graves of loved ones, flocking to the city's numerous graveyards in the dead of night on the new moon. The bulwark is maintained as long as no ghost goes forgotten and goes hungry.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983316#post983316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what the Huntsmen and enemy courts do to cause the Bulwark to fail is to cause Mardi Gras to fail, get the parade cancelled, have police crack down on public nudity, cut off the cities supply of booze, <b>stir up hurricanes so no one visits, </b>discourage the religious from observing the spiritual elements of Mardi Gras. In other words they try and sabotage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this? Do not do this. It's in poor taste. 1e's Miami writeup didn't go there and you definitely shouldn't try for that in New Orleans of all places, given the last decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:44:48-07:00","id":983596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983369#post983369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a step back, think on what's important to the city's history and what would be important to the Changelings.<b> Honoring the dead</b> and <b>food </b>are the two things I think of, first. I'm envisioning a frequent (monthly, perhaps) ritual that borrows from Dia de los Muertos, where changelings place offerings of food at the graves of loved ones, flocking to the city's numerous graveyards in the dead of night on the new moon. The bulwark is maintained as long as no ghost goes forgotten and goes hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually would encourage a lot of crossover chronicles. Sin-Eaters, especially. And if it's a crossover setting you are making, I might suggest looking up this hunter group from a fan supplement called Skin and Bones? It specialized in fighting the undead and Prometheans from what I recall.<br /> <br /> On the Mardi Gras side, I am contemplating a revision to a 1E Entitlement - the Magistrates of the Wax Mask - for a possible character. He (or she) would be the one to organize the ritual for the dead <i>and</i> the Courts' contribution to Mardi Gras. And I can see him being a Gravewright, possibly a Beast or even a Grimm.<br /> <br /> As for Mardi Gras itself, maybe it's a time where the Huntsmen and Gentry are especially active? Not to mention the local Goblin Market/s could be out in the city, mingling with locals for the festivities. Heck, you could even play up the food side by having it be the period where several rare Goblin Fruits are known to be in season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:05:23-07:00","id":983678,"title":"","content":"If you're going to have a regular ritual, I'd base it on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Joseph%27s_Day#United_States_of_America\" target=\"_blank\">Feast of St. Joseph's.</a> Plus you can have fun with St. Joseph's Bread.<br /> <br /> Also, ah, Indians in conjunction with Mardi Gras <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mardi_Gras_Indians\" target=\"_blank\">might have a different connotation than you're thinking.</a> I'd call it the Plaquemine Krewe if I were you.<br /> <br /> Just your friendly neighborhood Cajun giving some quick two cents, though. Everything else I've read looks really fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:15:57-07:00","id":983944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983369#post983369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this option really ignores lots of opportunities and goes with the first thing anyone associates with New Orleans.<br /> <br /> Take a step back, think on what's important to the city's history and what would be important to the Changelings.<b> Honoring the dead</b> and <b>food </b>are the two things I think of, first. I'm envisioning a frequent (monthly, perhaps) ritual that borrows from Dia de los Muertos, where changelings place offerings of food at the graves of loved ones, flocking to the city's numerous graveyards in the dead of night on the new moon. The bulwark is maintained as long as no ghost goes forgotten and goes hungry.Okay, this? Do not do this. It's in poor taste. 1e's Miami writeup didn't go there and you definitely shouldn't try for that in New Orleans of all places, given the last decade.</div> </div> </div> </div> Making it about honoring the dead steps too much on Sin Eaters toes.<br /> <br /> And I don't agree that the hurricane is in poor taste, I've seen TV shows bring it up, its a major point in the cities history, it makes no sense to ignore Katrina, anymore then Scion ignores WWII, which btw way was a far more horrific event. I mean Katrina was sad, but not evil, and bouncing back from that is heart warming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:49:49-07:00","id":983952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983944#post983944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making it about honoring the dead steps too much on Sin Eaters toes.<br /> <br /> And I don't agree that the hurricane is in poor taste, I've seen TV shows bring it up, its a major point in the cities history, it makes no sense to ignore Katrina, anymore then Scion ignores WWII, which btw way was a far more horrific event. I mean Katrina was sad, but not evil, and bouncing back from that is heart warming.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) As if vampires, werewolves, mages, prometheans, hunters, mummies, and beasts somehow did not also honor the dead.<br /> <br /> Just because the Sin-Eaters are the ghost splat does not mean everything dealing with the dead belongs to them, particularly if the dead are a big enough cultural cornerstone in the area to warrant it, nevermind questions of the dead being such a damn busy thing that people feel they need to by the former Contracts of Shades and Spirits. And, oh, yeah, the Contract of Shades and Spirits was a thing, so dealing with ghosts and the dead has long intended to be an acceptable vector for Changeling.<br /> <br /> 2) You are, of course, allowed to disagree.<br /> <br /> But I don't think anyone here actually trusts your taste buds, so that would be your problem.<br /> <br /> That aside, it is extremely rude to reduce one of the bigger catastrophes of the last decade to &quot;My retreival service sent in a hurricane to steal some people&quot;. Sure, we're &quot;getting over it&quot;, but there's context to the ways we get over it. Making it a result of the Huntsmen is fucking dismissive as hell.<br /> <br /> 3) Speaking of, reducing New Orleans to Mardi Gras and the French Quarter is also fucking dismissive as hell. Thought you ought to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-08-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:17:22-07:00","id":984003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983952#post983952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) As if vampires, werewolves, mages, prometheans, hunters, mummies, and beasts somehow did not also honor the dead.<br /> <br /> Just because the Sin-Eaters are the ghost splat does not mean everything dealing with the dead belongs to them, particularly if the dead are a big enough cultural cornerstone in the area to warrant it, nevermind questions of the dead being such a damn busy thing that people feel they need to by the former Contracts of Shades and Spirits. And, oh, yeah, the Contract of Shades and Spirits was a thing, so dealing with ghosts and the dead has long intended to be an acceptable vector for Changeling.<br /> <br /> 2) You are, of course, allowed to disagree.<br /> <br /> But I don't think anyone here actually trusts your taste buds, so that would be your problem.<br /> <br /> That aside, it is extremely rude to reduce one of the bigger catastrophes of the last decade to &amp;quot;My retreival service sent in a hurricane to steal some people&amp;quot;. Sure, we're &amp;quot;getting over it&amp;quot;, but there's context to the ways we get over it. Making it a result of the Huntsmen is fucking dismissive as hell.<br /> <br /> 3) Speaking of, reducing New Orleans to Mardi Gras and the French Quarter is also fucking dismissive as hell. Thought you ought to know.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think Huntsmen can send Hurricanes, so clearly I didn't think it through, honestly it had just an off hand addition when I mentioned it. Feel free not to use Hurricanes. My original point wasn't really about Hurricanes.<br /> <br /> Did at anytime I say Mardi Gras was the only thing in New Orleans? It just makes a good Bulwark ritual to build courts around. Its a starting point to build around. <br /> <br /> Its easily graspable for people who don't live in New Orleans, an exciting point to plot around. Should one become in expert in every part of New Orleans, every landmark, every major ethinic group, every historical moment?<br /> <br /> Or you can keep it simple and interesting to start off with, focusing on Mardi Gras, and then build out from there once they get used to things.<br /> <br /> To use Toronto Freehold as an example Toronto doesn't begin and end in downtown Toronto, where Kensington Market, the CN Tower, and the start of Young Street all are, nor is multiculturalism the beginning and ending to the GTA, Toronto had history before Pierre Trudeau made Multiculturalism a thing, but do I expect the Changeling Toronto to try and encompass everything Toronto is or could be, alsolutely not, they picked some of the things that really stood out about Toronto, The its the most Multicultural Metropolitian City in the World, the CN Tower, Young Street, Kensington Market, is what they choose, but they said nothing about Scarbough, Etobiko, York Region, Peel Region, Halton Region, Durham Region, places like the Skydome, Sharon Temple, Canada's Wonderland, ect..., because you can't expect them to explore GTA in it totality, its too big, just as New Orleans.<br /> <br /> And Young Street doesn't start in Kensington Market, in fact fact Young Street doesn't go through Kensington Market at all, Spadina does. But its not a big deal, I can work around it by making the Hedge Goblin Market much bigger then Ironside Kensington Market.<br /> <br /> So you look for few key exciting ideas, and build from there. So no, I did not reduce New Orleans to Mardi Gras and the French Quarter, I just used it as a suggested focal point for the Bulwark and the Courts.<br /> <br /> As for Sin Eaters, he was already naming the Courts Krewes so focusing a court on Honoring the Dead is doubling down on Sin Eater turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:49:20-07:00","id":984114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984003#post984003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should one become in expert in every part of New Orleans, every landmark, every major ethinic group, every historical moment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... <i>yes. </i>If you are making a place into a setting, you ought to devote at least a bit of your time getting past the surface detail of that place and learning what makes it tick.<br /> <br /> As for infringing on Sin-Eater &quot;turf,&quot; they already said this was for a crossover campaign, not a Changeling one. It's already a place where their turfs blend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:20:33-07:00","id":984149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=983952#post983952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Speaking of, reducing New Orleans to Mardi Gras and the French Quarter is also fucking dismissive as hell. Thought you ought to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly get where you're coming from on this, what with Jazz, Creole tradition, Catholicism, New Orleans voodoo, and a torrid history of both racial and political corruption being part and parcel of NOLA's culture, but this is intended to be a game that, presumably, non-natives can enjoy. <br /> <br /> No one wants to play a game about how Jim Garrison won a Supreme Court case that guaranteed the right of the individual to defame the government without censure, regardless of the man's legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:28:33-07:00","id":984157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984149#post984149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly get where you're coming from on this, what with Jazz, Creole tradition, Catholicism, New Orleans voodoo, and a torrid history of both racial and political corruption being part and parcel of NOLA's culture, but this is intended to be a game that, presumably, non-natives can enjoy.<br /> <br /> No one wants to play a game about how Jim Garrison won a Supreme Court case that guaranteed the right of the individual to defame the government without censure, regardless of the man's legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tokyo's written so that non-natives can enjoy too, that doesn't stop it from not-pandering to the basest conceptions of Japanese culture.<br /> <br /> No one wants to play a game about how Jim Garrison won a Supreme Court case, but no one wants a Las Vegas game that that thinks all there is to the city is The Strip either. These portions of a city are not the whole city, and it's a disservice to both fans and inhabitants to treat it as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:29:29-07:00","id":984158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984114#post984114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... <i>yes. </i>If you are making a place into a setting, you ought to devote at least a bit of your time getting past the surface detail of that place and learning what makes it tick.<br /> <br /> As for infringing on Sin-Eater &quot;turf,&quot; they already said this was for a crossover campaign, not a Changeling one. It's already a place where their turfs blend.</div> </div> </div> </div> I did, I could have suggested just making it about getting drunk and flashing tits for beads, but I suggested exploring Mardi Gras including from its more religious back group via the Bulwark and the courts relationship to it, I did not try and design the whole setting, I made one suggestion for how the Bulwark could work.<br /> <br /> Okay then yeah it makes more sense if its a crossover setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-08-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:52:08-07:00","id":984166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984157#post984157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tokyo's written so that non-natives can enjoy too, that doesn't stop it from not-pandering to the basest conceptions of Japanese culture.<br /> <br /> No one wants to play a game about how Jim Garrison won a Supreme Court case, but no one wants a Las Vegas game that that thinks all there is to the city is The Strip either. These portions of a city are not the whole city, and it's a disservice to both fans and inhabitants to treat it as such.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I've seen several TV shows and movies about Los Vegas that are EXACTLY that, pretty much focused entirely on the strip.<br /> <br /> People want to focus on what makes a city cool and interesting.<br /> <br /> I'll point out the OP also was concidering a way to connect the Bulwark to Mardi Gras, I merely suggested another way to go about it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this has gotten riiduculus, what the fuck are you offended by?<br /> <br /> You don't like my idea, that's fine, no biggy, but please don't make me out to be somekind of asshole, because I'm not and that's not fair.<br /> <br /> New Orleans is a wonderful city with the rich tradition, and I've done it no harm to it or its reputation as a world class city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:49:24-07:00","id":984186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984157#post984157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tokyo's written so that non-natives can enjoy too, that doesn't stop it from not-pandering to the basest conceptions of Japanese culture.<br /> <br /> No one wants to play a game about how Jim Garrison won a Supreme Court case, but no one wants a Las Vegas game that that thinks all there is to the city is The Strip either. These portions of a city are not the whole city, and it's a disservice to both fans and inhabitants to treat it as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but no one wants to play in a Las Vegas game that DOESN'T have that as a large chunk of the game, either. Seriously, I ain't setting a game in Vegas and focusing on the residential area. The French Quarter isn't all there is to NOLA, but it is where the city began. All of its history began right there. It's the highest point in the city, it's the focus for much if not all of the tourism and culture that runs through the area. To say that New Orleans is only the French Quarter may be untrue, but from a metaphysical, spiritual, resonant, ley lined, hallowed, trod, dragon's nested, haunted standpoint, it very much is all there is that'll be contested ground for every supernatural force in the area.<br /> <br /> No one's going to fight over the residential area, <i>coullion</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-08-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:51:53-07:00","id":984212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984186#post984186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one's going to fight over the residential area, <i>coullion</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but consider: This is a game that is in no uncertain terms about finding your way home.<br /> <br /> <i>People <b>live in</b> the residential area</i>.<br /> <br /> Consider also: This is a setting where the supernatural is hidden and magical circumstances tend not to have a causative relation to major events.<br /> <br /> <i>Many of those circumstances are the result of forces that <b>exist outside of time</b>.</i><br /> <br /> Finally, consider that part of the reason that the supernatural doesn't tend to directly interface with major events is because it strains credibility to have human history on the major scale drawn from the particular focused efforts of some group of monsters.<br /> <br /> <i>Basing the failure of New Orleans's Bulwark on the ruination of <b>the annual nationally-renowned festival of Mardi Gras</b></i><i> is absurd on its face.</i><br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how the story implied by &quot;the Bulwark of New Orleans <i>is</i> Mardi Gras&quot; is only marginally less absurd than &quot;the sanctity of the Manhattan freehold depends on the successful completion of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:53:53-07:00","id":984213,"title":"","content":"Cities are not their tourist spots alone. You want to incorporate them, fine-I capitalized a shit ton on Paris as the city of Love and Lights in my own pursuits on the subject(And, worth noting, I consider mine the least of the four cities). But a city is not their tourist spots alone. There are deeper, weirder, more interesting settings beyond The Strip, the French Quarter, and stereotypes about Japanese culture, and we should always be willing to explore them.<br /> <br /> For fuck's sake, the major reason people love the Tokyo setting as it's been developing is how much it <i>does not play</i> to the pop-culture conception of Japan. If we can do that with that nation, we can aspire to more for others, particularly(what I imagine is the case here) our own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:28:55-07:00","id":984233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984212#post984212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is to say nothing of how the story implied by &quot;the Bulwark of New Orleans <i>is</i> Mardi Gras&quot; is only marginally less absurd than &quot;the sanctity of the Manhattan freehold depends on the successful completion of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then take it to Mamou. They have a great, not-nationally renowned festival of Mardi Gras <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wasn't arguing for the Bulwark being the &quot;successful completion of Mardi Gras in the actual city of New Orleans.&quot; I was arguing that the <i>Freehold's Courts</i> could focus on Mardi Gras and the French Quarter, since they've got to focus on <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> Here, you want some good advice, cheres? Here's your Krewe breakdown:<ul><li>Krewe of Carnivale: Court emotion - Celebration, court colors - green, Inauguration Day - Mardi Gras</li> <li>Krewe of Zydeco: Court emotion - Nostalgia, court colors - purple, Inauguration Day - Zydeco Festival</li> <li>Krewe of Hallows: Court emotion - Faith, court colors - gold, Inauguration Day - All Saint's Day</li> </ul>And here's your Bulwark:<br /> At the end of the Faithful time, the New Orleans' Freehold begins its new year at Mardi Gras. It is on this night that the Freehold eschews the Quarter and the lights of the city, for their Contract has come due. The Fae come wearing graceful, wicked masques, and the Lost must put on a show. They make floats, gather beads, hone their talents, and make a parade through the Hedge, marking their territory with every throw and every shout and every footfall. This event must be perfect each time, a culmination of a year's worth of planning and practice, for if they falter in even the slightest they shall fall before the next year's end.<br /> <br /> A bit rushed on the flavor-text, more than I'd like, but it's not <i>my</i> setting or <i>my </i>players that I'm trying to satisfy. At this point, it's not even the OP's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-09-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:08:03-07:00","id":984361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984212#post984212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but consider: This is a game that is in no uncertain terms about finding your way home.<br /> <br /> <i>People <b>live in</b> the residential area</i>.<br /> <br /> Consider also: This is a setting where the supernatural is hidden and magical circumstances tend not to have a causative relation to major events.<br /> <br /> <i>Many of those circumstances are the result of forces that <b>exist outside of time</b>.</i><br /> <br /> Finally, consider that part of the reason that the supernatural doesn't tend to directly interface with major events is because it strains credibility to have human history on the major scale drawn from the particular focused efforts of some group of monsters.<br /> <br /> <i>Basing the failure of New Orleans's Bulwark on the ruination of <b>the annual nationally-renowned festival of Mardi Gras</b></i><i> is absurd on its face.</i><br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how the story implied by &amp;quot;the Bulwark of New Orleans <i>is</i> Mardi Gras&amp;quot; is only marginally less absurd than &amp;quot;the sanctity of the Manhattan freehold depends on the successful completion of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Why couldn't it?<br /> <br /> Its just a ritual that maintains the magic that defends the freehold, as long as it takes enough effort to do, it works and protects the freehold, there is nothing wrong with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:08:39-07:00","id":984362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982457-2e-help-me-design-the-courts-of-new-orleans?p=984233#post984233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then take it to Mamou. They have a great, not-nationally renowned festival of Mardi Gras <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wasn't arguing for the Bulwark being the &amp;quot;successful completion of Mardi Gras in the actual city of New Orleans.&amp;quot; I was arguing that the <i>Freehold's Courts</i> could focus on Mardi Gras and the French Quarter, since they've got to focus on <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> Here, you want some good advice, cheres? Here's your Krewe breakdown:<ul><li>Krewe of Carnivale: Court emotion - Celebration, court colors - green, Inauguration Day - Mardi Gras</li> <li>Krewe of Zydeco: Court emotion - Nostalgia, court colors - purple, Inauguration Day - Zydeco Festival</li> <li>Krewe of Hallows: Court emotion - Faith, court colors - gold, Inauguration Day - All Saint's Day</li> </ul>And here's your Bulwark:<br /> At the end of the Faithful time, the New Orleans' Freehold begins its new year at Mardi Gras. It is on this night that the Freehold eschews the Quarter and the lights of the city, for their Contract has come due. The Fae come wearing graceful, wicked masques, and the Lost must put on a show. They make floats, gather beads, hone their talents, and make a parade through the Hedge, marking their territory with every throw and every shout and every footfall. This event must be perfect each time, a culmination of a year's worth of planning and practice, for if they falter in even the slightest they shall fall before the next year's end.<br /> <br /> A bit rushed on the flavor-text, more than I'd like, but it's not <i>my</i> setting or <i>my </i>players that I'm trying to satisfy. At this point, it's not even the OP's.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}